 # UnderWeb X changelog
 
+## 0.5.2-rc11 — OSC Lab 3: music, weather and statuses together
+
+Root causes fixed from 0.5.0:
+- Two senders ran at once (the old 4-second auto-broadcast and the OSC2 rotation), sending duplicate and conflicting chatbox messages. Now there is one scheduler.
+- Modules replaced each other (one screen at a time). Now every enabled module renders together, in the order you choose.
+- Statuses, queue, modes and weather settings were never saved, and weather was only fetched when you pressed the button. All settings now persist, and weather loads on startup and every 20 minutes.
+- OSC only started after opening the UnderWeb page, and its timers stopped when you left it. OSC Lab now starts with the app.
+- Music progress came from a stale Windows media timestamp. UWX now extrapolates from the time Windows last updated it, and prefers whatever app is actually playing (Spotify first).
+
+What you get:
+- Live preview showing exactly what VRChat will show, with character and line counts (144 / 9 limits).
+- Per-module on/off, ordering, and editable layouts with tokens ({artist}, {title}, {time}, {duration}, {temp}, {condition}…).
+- Statuses: add, edit order, star to rotate, sequential or random (no repeats until all have shown), rotation interval.
+- Sending rules: never more than once every 2.5s; sends right away when the track, status, weather or heart rate changes; music progress refresh every 10s (adjustable); keep-alive every 25s; one clear message when you turn it off. "Hide now" clears instantly.
+- "Sent to VRChat" log shows every message actually sent and why.
+- Privacy: ZIP stays on this PC and is never in the chatbox; weather service gets coordinates rounded to ~10 km. World name is off by default.
+- 19 new unit tests for the composer, scheduler, status rotation, media timeline and settings migration.
+
 ## 0.5.1-rc10 — Group Tools + everyday Instance Inviter
 
 - Instance Inviter now works in any instance VRChat lets you invite into (public, group, Friends+, Invite+, your own), not only approved group instances. Uses VRCX's own invite rules, so blocked instances show the reason instead of failing.
